                <pb facs="0532" n="432" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg432"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">662.116 Lard/28: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-25T16:00:00+01:00">June 25, 1934—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 25—1:03 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>120. Agriculture Attaché in telegram No. 477, June 23 to the Department of
                    Agriculture announces prohibition July all lard imports except from countries
                    having special agreements.</p>
                <p>Multiplication import and export restrictions points to early establishment of
                    central foreign trade control.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodd</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
